From: Darrel Griet <dgriet@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Jul 2026 13:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] omapfb: minnow-panel: Use 60Hz as the normal-mode refresh rate

0017 restores 60Hz in the static SSD2848 init sequence, but the runtime
refresh-rate manager overrides it: on every wake from ambient mode back
to normal (DISPLAY_AMBIENT_ON -> DISPLAY_ENABLE) the driver calls
minnow_panel_set_default_fps(), which re-writes the SSD2848 VTCM pixel-
clock-ratio register [0x0010] to the REFRESH_RATE_45HZ table entry. Since
the watch cycles through ambient mode while idle, the panel settles back
at 45Hz after the first ambient wake.

Point the "default" (normal-mode) rate at the existing REFRESH_RATE_60HZ
table entry so normal operation stays at 60Hz. Ambient (30Hz) and dock
(60Hz) rates are unchanged. Depends on 0017 (OMAP DISPC pixel clock and
the init-sequence VTCM ratio must also be 60Hz).

Trade-off: higher display power draw. Revert (with 0017) for 45Hz.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [minnow board/panel specific]

---
--- a/drivers/video/omap2/displays/panel-minnow.c
+++ b/drivers/video/omap2/displays/panel-minnow.c
@@ -629,7 +629,7 @@
 #define minnow_panel_set_lowest_fps(mpd)	\
 		minnow_panel_set_refresh_rate_mlocked(mpd, REFRESH_RATE_30HZ)
 #define minnow_panel_set_default_fps(mpd)	\
-		minnow_panel_set_refresh_rate_mlocked(mpd, REFRESH_RATE_45HZ)
+		minnow_panel_set_refresh_rate_mlocked(mpd, REFRESH_RATE_60HZ)
 #define minnow_panel_set_dock_fps(mpd)	\
 		minnow_panel_set_refresh_rate_mlocked(mpd, REFRESH_RATE_60HZ)
 static int minnow_panel_set_refresh_rate_mlocked(struct minnow_panel_data *mpd,
